e(timeout=0) time out every call instantly'","Plan invokes the ACLI precedent: 'mirrors reconciler.jira_cli_timeout' and 'the acli_subprocess.py pattern'"],"finding":"The proposed timeout validator _as_float(v, k, minimum=0.0) admits an explicit 0, which would make proc.communicate(timeout=0) time out every render instantly and silently degrade all safe-run segments to verbatim — the exact hazard the ACLI precedent this plan invokes guards against by treating a non-positive value as 'unset, fall back to default' (_acli_call_timeout, acli_subprocess.py:72-89).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f37c14181a0d1cf2b","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / config bullet: `_as_float(v, k, minimum=0.0)`; AC line 3 (timeout)","norm_id":"n3f5a1b31f9639bc0","priority":0.2933,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An operator sets reconciler.dc_pandoc_timeout_s=0 (e.g. intending 'disable timeout'), and every safe-run render silently falls back to verbatim Markdown, dropping all wiki richness with no error."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Have the wiki_render consumer resolve the timeout as `value if value > 0 else 10.0` (the ACLI precedent), so an explicit 0 or negative value falls back to the default rather than instantly timing out every render.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the 'pandoc exposes no --server/daemon' claim (pandoc ships a `pandoc server` / pandoc-server JSON-API mode) and re-justify choosing per-run batching over a persistent server on accurate grounds (e.g., HTTP/sandbox operational cost or the change-gated no-op gate bounding spawn volume).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'pandoc 3.9 exposes no `--server`/daemon, so a persistent server is out of scope.'","Retrieved pandoc.org/pandoc-server.html: 'pandoc-server is a web server that can perform pandoc conversions.'","Retrieved pandoc.org/demo example33: 'if you call pandoc with server as the first argument, it will start up a web server with a JSON API. This server exposes most of the conversion functionality of pandoc.'","This parenthetical is load-bearing: it is the plan's sole justification for choosing per-run batching over a persistent-server architecture (T1(a)/(c))."],"finding":"The plan's stated reason for ruling out a persistent-server alternative — 'pandoc 3.9 exposes no --server/daemon, so a persistent server is out of scope' — rests on an inaccurate capability assertion. Retrieved pandoc documentation shows pandoc ships a `server` subcommand / `pandoc-server` mode that runs a persistent web server exposing conversions over a JSON HTTP API (existing since pandoc 2.x, current in 3.x). While the literal flag `--server` may not exist (it is invoked as `pandoc server` or via a `pandoc-server` symlink), the persistent-conversion-server capability the plan denies does exist and would directly address the ~0.3s/field spawn tax that motivates this story. The prior-art dismissal should either be corrected/removed or the server option should be evaluated and rejected on accurate grounds (e.g., HTTP-API operational cost, sandbox constraints, or that the change-gated no-op gate already bounds spawn volume).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa47126702fcc0efe","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section, batching bullet parenthetical: '(pandoc 3.9 exposes no --server/daemon, so a persistent server is out of scope.)'","norm_id":"n7ea97ae886411ec9","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Reviewer/author later discovers `pandoc server` exists and questions whether batching was the right architecture","A future performance regression re-opens the server-vs-batch decision with no accurate record of why server was rejected"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Replace the parenthetical with an accurate rejection, e.g.: 'pandoc does expose a persistent server (`pandoc server` / pandoc-server JSON HTTP API), but a long-lived server is out of scope here because [operational cost / the change-gated rich_sha gate already bounds spawn volume to changed bodies]; contiguous-safe-run batching amortizes the residual per-render spawn cost without a resident process.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without